Title: Lab 7: Boyle's law from measured data
Author: Math++ pipeline test (chemistry)

%{
**Pipeline expectations.** The expected product is $nRT \approx 99.15\ \mathrm J$. The linear fit of $P$ against $1/V$ gives a slope $\approx 99.2\ \mathrm J$ (tolerance $0.5$), an intercept near $0$, and $R^2 > 0.999$. The amount of gas is recovered as $n \approx 0.0400\ \mathrm{mol}$. Units: $\mathrm{kPa} \cdot \mathrm L = \mathrm J$ must simplify.
%}

## Setup
